 stopped setting record lows","change":"San Francisco's days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 64\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>64\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 64\u00b0F, and the record is 76\u00b0F (1995). The low of <strong>55\u00b0F</strong> was the 8th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 82 since 1945.","t_rec":"San Francisco has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If San Francisco's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, San Francisco has set <strong class=\"sig\">6 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 121 that chance alone would give, and <strong>155 record highs</strong>, more than the 121 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (57). San Francisco's all-time high is 105\u00b0F, on June 14, 2000.","t_chg":"San Francisco's days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 78 complete years: San Francisco's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.64\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.54 to +0.73), about +5.0\u00b0F since 1946. San Francisco's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.35\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.22 to +0.47), about +2.8\u00b0F since 1946.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in 10 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"San Francisco's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.02 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 19.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 1983 (38.34 in); the driest, 2013 (3.38 in). San Francisco almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 13 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}